we begin this half hour with news of yet  another mass shooting this time in  norway police in oslo the capitol say at  least two people were killed when a  gunman known to police opened fire  outside a bar that is popular among the  city's lgbtq plus community nearly two  dozen people were injured the attack  happened just ahead of a gay pride  parade ian lee is in our london bureau  with the very latest ian good morning  good morning dana in recent hours  norwegian police have declared the  attack an act of terrorism one  eyewitness described a man arriving  outside the bar around one in the  morning he was holding a bag then pulled  out a gun and started shooting bullets  hit multiple people as well as nearby  businesses shattering glass windows and  sending debris flying through the air  another witness described how the gunman  took careful aim before shooting his  victims he then opened fire at two other  nearby locations before police  eventually arrived and arrested him  authorities are describing the suspect  as a 42-year-old norwegian citizen of  iranian descent he's now being charged  with murder and acts of terrorism police  recovered a gun and an automatic weapon  at the scene as of now officials don't  believe anyone else was involved but  today was supposed to be oslo's pride  parade authorities don't yet know if the  shooting is connected but there is an  increased security presence in the city  the parade and other pride festivities  have now been canceled following advice  from the police jeff  all right ian lee with the latest on  this shooting in norway ian thank you  very much
 

